Binary search is a serchiing method used to search for a specific element known as target in an already sorted array.
The algorithm which binary search follows is as follows :-
->Sort the array if not already.
->initialise 2 variable-
    >int left = 0;
    >int right = (size of array)-1;
->Then we find the mid point index of the array by using a simple mathematical formula -
    >int mid = left + ( right-left )/2;
->Now we check if the given target is equal to the mid point index value or not,
    >if yes, mid index is returned and the execution is complete.
    >if no,
      >we check if the value if target is > or < the mid index value.
        >if > then we check the right half of the array (left = mid + 1)
        >if < then we check the left half of the array (right = mid - 1)
->Then we keep on dividing the halves into more halves and repeat the same process untill we reach the target.
->The time omplexity of this search methond is O(log n).

-> The function of the binary search is given below - 
<----------------------------------------------->
int binarySearch(vector<int>& a, int key) {
    sort(a.begin(), a.end());
    int left = 0, right = a.size() - 1;

    while (left <= right) {
        int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

        if (a[mid] == key)
            return mid;

        if (a[mid] < key)
            left = mid + 1;
        else
            right = mid - 1;
    }
    return -1;
}
<-------------------------------------------------->

